// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root cause of prior failure: GenerateWithManagedSpan internally checks
// IsCompletePrefix after every constrained token and immediately calls
// CloseConstrainedSpan.  For an arithmetic-expression grammar, a single
// identifier like "n0" is already complete, so the span closed after one
// token and produced wrong single-variable answers instead of full expressions
// like "n0 * (r + 1)**d".
//
// Fix: two-phase explicit loop.
//   Phase 1 – Unconstrained reasoning in plain text until "<<" is observed
//   (using RenderedEndsWith), EOS, or budget.
//   Phase 2 – Constrained token generation inside the span using
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep, but NO IsCompletePrefix check mid-loop.  The
//   span remains open until the model emits EOS (signalling "done") or the
//   step budget runs out.
//   Post-loop – If the span is still open and its content is a complete parse,
//   emit ">>" via CloseConstrainedSpan (one extra step, guarded by steps < maxSteps).
// AppendTaskGuidance instructs the model to finish ALL chain-of-thought in
// plain text before opening "<<", and to write a complete Python-style
// symbolic expression as the single final answer.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 (parser_validity):
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Phase 1: While !insideConstrainedOut the implication is vacuously true.
//   When we transition (RenderedEndsWith detects "<<") we set
//   currentConstrainedOut := [] and parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by the
//   method precondition.  EOS breaks the loop without touching span state.
//
//   Phase 2: AdaptiveConstrainedStep either returns eosToken or a token that
//   is parser-valid at currentConstrainedOut.  On EOS we break without
//   modifying span state, so the induction hypothesis carries forward.  On a
//   non-EOS token, AppendConstrainedToken appends it to both generated and
//   currentConstrainedOut; its postcondition guarantees the updated
//   currentConstrainedOut remains parser-valid.
//
//   Post-loop close: we call CloseConstrainedSpan only when
//   parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) holds (a guard we check
//   explicitly), which is stronger than IsValidPrefix.  Afterwards
//   insideConstrainedOut = false, making the implication vacuously true.
//
// Invariant 2 (progress):
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Phase 1: Each iteration increments steps by 1 before any append.  On EOS,
//   no token is appended; on a normal token, generated grows by exactly 1.
//   Either way |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved.
//
//   Phase 2: Each iteration increments steps by 1.  On EOS we break with no
//   append; on a non-EOS token AppendConstrainedToken appends exactly one
//   token to generated.  Both branches preserve the bound.
//
//   Post-loop close: guarded by steps < maxSteps, so after steps := steps + 1
//   we have steps <= maxSteps.  CloseConstrainedSpan appends ">>" (one token)
//   to generated, so |generated| grows by 1 and steps grows by 1, maintaining
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

